   "source": [
    "## 0.3 Clean and derive core fields\n",
    "\n",
    "We keep the original CPMIP columns but add a few convenience fields:\n",
    "\n",
    "- `model_family`: a coarse grouping key (`Model-name`), used to keep \"comparable model classes\"\n",
    "  comparisons honest — you should not compare, say, an atmosphere-only configuration against a\n",
    "  fully coupled ESM without accounting for that difference.\n",
    "- `energy_JPSY` / `cost_CHSY`: numeric, coerced versions of the two main CPMIP cost metrics\n",
    "  (joules per simulated year; core-hours per simulated year).\n",
    "- `log10_energy`, `log10_cost`: log-scaled versions, since these metrics span several orders\n",
    "  of magnitude across platforms and resolutions.\n",
    "- `resolution_total`: a simple proxy for total resolution (atmosphere + ocean grid points),\n",
    "  useful for the energy-adjusted interpretation section.\n",
    "\n",
    "Adjust the column-name mapping in `COLMAP` if your own data uses different headers."
   ]
  },
